    {"id": "example:has-repeat", "kind": "code", "lang": "python", "front": "Has Repeat\n\nReturn true if any value in the list appears twice.", "back": "Keep what you have seen; a repeat is a value already kept.", "answer": "def has_repeat(values):\n    seen = set()\n    for v in values:\n        if v in seen:\n            return True\n        seen.add(v)\n    return False", "harness": "try:\n    (has_repeat)\nexcept NameError:\n    raise Exception(\"__signature_mismatch__\")\n\n__results__ = []\ndef __case__(label, expected, actual):\n    __results__.append([label, repr(expected), repr(actual)])\n\n__case__(\"has_repeat([1, 2, 1])\", True, has_repeat([1, 2, 1]))\n__case__(\"has_repeat([1, 2, 3])\", False, has_repeat([1, 2, 3]))\n__case__(\"has_repeat([])\", False, has_repeat([]))\n", "complexity": "O(n) time", "patterns": [{"slug": "seen-set", "name": "Seen set", "complexity": "O(n) time", "nudge": "What do you keep as you walk?", "steps": ["Remember", "Walk"], "notes": [{"id": 1, "step": 0, "pseudo": "seen = empty set", "hint": "What do you keep?", "why": "The values to the left."}, {"id": 2, "step": 1, "pseudo": "for v in values:", "hint": "How do you walk?", "why": "Once."}, {"id": 3, "step": 1, "pseudo": "    if v in seen: return True", "hint": "When is it a repeat?", "why": "When it was kept before."}, {"id": 4, "step": 1, "pseudo": "    add v to seen", "hint": "And otherwise?", "why": "Keep it for the values after."}, {"id": 5, "step": 1, "pseudo": "return False", "hint": "At the end?", "why": "No repeat was found."}], "lines": [{"given": "def has_repeat(values):"}, {"text": "seen = set()", "indent": 4, "notes": [1]}, {"text": "for v in values:", "indent": 4, "notes": [2]}, {"text": "if v in seen:", "indent": 8, "notes": [3]}, {"text": "return True", "indent": 12, "notes": [3]}, {"text": "seen.add(v)", "indent": 8, "notes": [4]}, {"text": "return False", "indent": 4, "notes": [5]}]}], "tags": ["drills", "python"]}
